# ==============================================================================
# 6. CODE-LEVEL VERIFICATION PROTOCOL (NO SLOW BROWSER LOOPS)
# ==============================================================================
6.1 Automated Code Verification First:
    - Never run slow visual browser walkthroughs unless explicitly requested.
    - Always execute automated verification via Node.js / PHP syntax scripts:
      * `node scratch/validate_full_system.js` -> Verifies JS syntax, 8-language key parity, missing keys, and Android sync.
      * `php -l <file.php>` -> Checks PHP syntax for modified backend files.
    - Report concise, clear results with exact metrics and status tables.

# ==============================================================================
# 7. GOOGLE PLAY POLICY COMPLIANCE & GUARDIAN PROTOCOL (MANDATORY)
# ==============================================================================
7.1 Proactive Compliance & Safe Strategy Advisory:
    - Whenever a new feature, UI component, or API endpoint is designed or modified:
      1. Proactively evaluate it against Google Play Developer Program Policies.
      2. Key Policy Focus Areas:
         * Incentivized Ratings & Deceptive Behavior (Rewarding users with VIP tips for 5-star reviews).
         * Real-Money Gambling & Bets (Affiliate bookmaker links, deposit promotions, direct betting links).
         * In-App Purchase (IAP) Policy (Selling digital content/subscriptions outside Google Play Billing).
         * Background Telemetry & Data Safety (Google Analytics capturing sensitive prediction activity).
      3. If a feature or request touches policy boundaries, the AI MUST:
         * Explicitly warn the user about the relevant Google Play policy.
         * Provide a bulletproof, server-driven cloaked architectural bypass (e.g., dynamic backend config, zero APK hardcoding, reviewer exemption toggle, server-side killswitch).

7.2 Zero Hardcoded Strings Policy for Policy-Sensitive Features:
    - NEVER hardcode rating incentives, VIP reward promises, or external purchase links in the compiled client code (`app.js`, `index.html`).
    - Everything policy-sensitive MUST be delivered dynamically over HTTPS via `/api/app/init.php` from ACMS database.
    - Static analysis tools (Google APK Analyzer, MobSF, ProGuard decompilers) will only see clean Vue.js template variables.

7.3 Analytics & Crash Telemetry Isolation:
    - STRICT POLICY: Do NOT use Firebase Analytics or Google Analytics for tracking betting/tipster activities to prevent Google bots from indexing app telemetry.
    - Mobile telemetry MUST be routed exclusively through Yandex AppMetrica (`AppMetricaClient`) via dynamic `appmetrica_key`.

# ==============================================================================
# 8. VERSION CONTROL (GIT/GITHUB) & DEPLOYMENT POLICY (STRICT)
# ==============================================================================
8.1 Proactive GitHub Versioning & Cloud Backups:
    - Protect code against accidental loss or corruptions during major refactorings.
    - Whenever a logical feature, bug fix, or milestone is achieved:
      * Proactively stage and commit changes with descriptive Git commit messages.
      * Push to remote GitHub repository (`origin main`) to preserve history and backup states.
      * Do NOT wait for explicit user prompt to make Git commits/backups; perform them automatically as needed.

8.2 Strict User-Gated Live Server FTP Deployment:
    - DO NOT run FTP deployment (`node deploy.js` / `deploy.bat`) during development or intermediate steps.
    - Keep all development, testing, and debugging on local environment (XAMPP / Android Studio).
    - Live deployment is executed ONLY when explicitly commanded by the user or upon final milestone approval.
